# Staged specs are digested, and a digest over bytes that change on checkout
# is a digest that only validates on the machine that wrote it.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-09: tools/hpc3/runs/code-style-gen-v2-base.json is stored
# in git with LF (blob 2cae397c...) and checked out on Windows with CRLF
# (ffe2e671...), and code-style-specs-v2-stage.json records the CRLF value --
# because that is what was actually staged to /pub. So that manifest is
# correct about what it staged and NOT reproducible from a Linux checkout.
#
# The seed-0 pair is deliberately NOT renormalised here. Those exact bytes
# produced the v2 generation jobs 55809956/55809960, and changing them would
# make the committed digests disagree with the artifacts on /pub -- rewriting
# the provenance of a finished run to tidy a filename convention.
#
# The seed-axis specs added the same day are held to the stricter rule, so
# their digests mean the same thing on every machine.
runs/code-style-gen-v2-base-s?.json -text
runs/code-style-gen-v2-candidate-s?.json -text
runs/code-style-specs-v2-seeds-stage.json -text
